{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A lamp of contempt</b> — the lamed is superfluous, and it is from: אם בפידו להם שוע (if his cry came to them in his trouble) — on account of the trouble that came upon him, contempt dwells, as in: ובוז משפחות במחשבת השאנן (and contempt of families in the thought of the secure one)." "<b>For ready relief</b> — as in: אולי יתעשת האלהים (perhaps Elohim will relieve). אבדו עשתנותיו (his devices perished)." "<b>Prepared for those whose foot slips</b> — and this is a thing that a man brings about such that his foot slips, as in the matter of: ואני כמעט נטיו רגלי (and I, my foot nearly slipped)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:29.883652407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}